{
  "_about": [
    "AudioBooth decode proof manifest. One row per app request, in the order the Go generator issues them.",
    "callSite is the literal path string from the pinned AudioBooth source; the 45 strings in callSites are the coverage denominator.",
    "decode is the type the call site passes to NetworkRequest<T>. 'Data' means the app skips decoding and any 2xx succeeds.",
    "Placeholders {name} are filled from values captured out of earlier responses, the way the app chains ids.",
    "A string value that is exactly '{name}' is replaced by the captured value with its JSON type (number stays a number).",
    "Every request carries Content-Type: application/json and Authorization: Bearer <token> (NetworkService.buildURLRequest) unless auth is false.",
    "Query values are strings, as the app builds [String: String] queries.",
    "nonEmpty lists dotted JSON paths (numeric segments index arrays) that must be non-empty arrays or strings, checked by the key the app reads. An empty path means the body itself.",
    "Every captured value X also yields XB64, its base64 encoding, which is how the app builds filter=<group>.<base64> values."
  ],
